settings.local.json

# Jess's global gitexcludes ignores .tool-versions (a sensible default: tool
# pins are usually personal). Here it's the opposite — the asdf pin is the
# thing that keeps every one of Jess's computers on the same Ruby, so it has
# to be tracked. A repo .gitignore outranks core.excludesFile, so this wins.
!.tool-versions
.claude/worktrees/

# The importer's workspace: per-session scan results (SessionScan::Cache) and
# the listing page it generates. Both are derived from Jess's own conversation
# logs — private data that must never land in this public repo — and both are
# rebuildable from the logs, so there's nothing here worth tracking.
.importer/
